4
Results
4.1
How common is the gap?
Table 2 reports the audit over both corpora. Three findings, of which
one does not replicate.
Most parameters carry no machine-checkable constraint at
all. Across 721,320 public parameters, 7.5% declare an enumeration
and 15.2% declare any machine constraint whatsoever. Whatever
governs the remaining 85%, no validator can see it. A further 29.4%
